    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d632-a8">

                <pb facs="0531" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg415"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 262.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to my note of the 22d
                    instant in regard to the detention in Italy of naturalized American citizens of
                    Italian origin, and to my previous notes and conversations on the subject, I
                    have the honor to inform your excellency that I have received today telegraphic
                    instructions to request that permission to return to the United States be
                    granted to Joseph Rocco Casazza, a naturalized American citizen, detained at
                    Genoa, accompanied by his wife and child. It is understood that Casazza has
                    tuberculosis and came to Italy for his health.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas Nelson Page</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
